-- src:8967 | that agreement is lawful;
@ref s 76F(2)(a) no purchase is lawful where the requirements are not satisfied (src:8962-8967)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      directors IS A Party
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76B and s 76F the company purchases or acquires its shares within the authority while it is solvent` MEANS
    IF `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (IF `the company is a public company`
          THEN PARTY company
               SHANT `s 76B(9)(c) the company becomes entitled to exercise the rights attached to the shares, so that they are purchased or acquired`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST FULFILLED   -- closed route, not a breach: the purchase is not lawful (s 76F(2)(a), src:8965-8967), a nullity laid on no named party; the officer's offence is s 76F(3), encoded below
          ELSE PARTY company
               SHANT `s 76B(7) lodge a copy of the resolution and a notice of purchase or acquisition with the Registrar`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST FULFILLED)   -- closed route, not a breach: the purchase is not lawful (s 76F(2)(a), src:8965-8967), a nullity laid on no named party; the officer's offence is s 76F(3), encoded below
    ELSE (IF `the company is a public company`
          THEN PARTY company
               MAY `s 76B(9)(c) the company becomes entitled to exercise the rights attached to the shares, so that they are purchased or acquired`
               WITHIN `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires`
               HENCE (`s 76B(9)(b) and s 76G(1) after the purchase the directors of a public company lodge the notice of purchase and the company reduces its share capital or profits` company directors `the company is a public company` `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)
               LEST FULFILLED
          ELSE PARTY company
               MAY `s 76B(7) lodge a copy of the resolution and a notice of purchase or acquisition with the Registrar`
               WITHIN `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires`
               HENCE (`s 76B(9)(b) and s 76G(1) after the purchase the directors of a public company lodge the notice of purchase and the company reduces its share capital or profits` company directors `the company is a public company` `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)
               LEST FULFILLED)

§ `Section 76B(9)(a): after the resolution`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D or 76E is passed; counting="within 30 days after the passing of a resolution", the integer line being the count of days with the last day day 30 (sg-periods P1, P2); the purchase window runs in parallel from the same day 0 (RAND) and is the rule above
-- FORK: s 76B(9)(a) | the lodging of the copy and the purchase are two parts of one rule that run together, each from day 0 (RAND), because (a) runs from the resolution and not from the purchase | the lodging chained after the purchase through HENCE
-- src:8459 | (9) Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by
-- src:8460 | it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E —
-- src:8462 | (a) within 30 days after the passing of a resolution mentioned
-- src:8463 | in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E (as the case may be) the
-- src:8464 | directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a
-- src:8465 | copy of the resolution;
@ref s 76B(9)(a) the copy of the resolution (src:8459-8465)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      directors IS A Party
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76B(9)(a) after the resolution the directors of a public company lodge its copy and the company purchases within the authority` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN ((PARTY directors
           MUST `s 76B(9)(a) lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar`
           WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY directors BECAUSE "the directors of the public company did not lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar within 30 days after it was passed")
          RAND (`s 76B and s 76F the company purchases or acquires its shares within the authority while it is solvent` company directors `the company is a public company` `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires` `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`))
    ELSE (`s 76B and s 76F the company purchases or acquires its shares within the authority while it is solvent` company directors `the company is a public company` `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` `the days from the resolution to the day the authority expires` `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)

§ `Section 76C: the off-market purchase on an equal access scheme`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day of the general meeting at which the company authorises the equal access scheme; counting=silent for the authority (the text sets no time for the meeting); the steps after it count as the two rules above state, the purchase window ending on the expiry date the notice specifies (s 76C(2)(c)), n being DATE_SERIAL of the expiry date minus DATE_SERIAL of the meeting date
-- FORK: s 76C(2)(c) | where the expiry date is later than the date the next annual general meeting is or is required to be held, the authority step is still open but nothing follows it, no copy to lodge and no purchase window | the authority valid up to the stated expiry date, or the resolution not passed at all
-- FORK: s 76C(1) | the authority is "authorised in advance by the company in general meeting" and the text names no majority, so the step is a MAY of the company with no resolution type | an ordinary resolution
-- src:8511 | 76C.—(1) A company, whether or not it is listed on an approved
-- src:8512 | exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore,
-- src:8513 | may make a purchase or acquisition of its own shares otherwise than
-- src:8514 | on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange
-- src:8515 | outside Singapore (called in this section an off‑market purchase) if
-- src:8516 | the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal
-- src:8517 | access scheme authorised in advance by the company in general
-- src:8518 | meeting.
@ref s 76C(1) the authority for an off-market purchase on an equal access scheme (src:8511-8518)
-- src:8532 | (c) specify a date on which the authority is to expire, being a
-- src:8533 | date that must not be later than the date on which the next
-- src:8534 | annual general meeting of the company is or is required by
-- src:8535 | law to be held, whichever is the earlier; and
@ref s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date of the authority (src:8532-8535)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      directors IS A Party
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is an off-market purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the general meeting that authorises the scheme` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76C the company in general meeting authorises an equal access scheme in advance and the lodging and the purchase follow` MEANS
    IF `s 76C(1) the company may make an off-market purchase or acquisition of its own shares` `the purchase or acquisition is an off-market purchase` `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with an equal access scheme` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `s 76C(2)(c) the expiry date is not later than the date of the next annual general meeting` `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
          THEN PARTY company
               MAY `s 76C(1) the company in general meeting authorises the equal access scheme in advance`
               HENCE (`s 76B(9)(a) after the resolution the directors of a public company lodge its copy and the company purchases within the authority` company directors `the company is a public company` `the shares are cancelled under section 76B(5) and not held in treasury under section 76H` ((DATE_SERIAL `the date specified in the notice on which the authority is to expire`) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the date of the general meeting that authorises the scheme`)) `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)
          ELSE PARTY company
               MAY `s 76C(1) the company in general meeting authorises the equal access scheme in advance`
               HENCE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 76D: the selective off-market purchase`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day of the meeting at which the special resolution is passed; counting="not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting" for the inspection (s 76D(7)(a)): the 15 days run back from day 0, so they are checked by the existing gate from the two DATE inputs and are not a step of the trace; the consent of s 76D(2A) comes "before passing the special resolution" and is likewise a gate input; the steps after the resolution count as the rules above state
