§ `Section 76E(1): no market purchase without advance authority`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company makes a purchase or acquisition of its own shares on a securities exchange; counting=silent (the bar has no time limit; whether the purchase was authorised in advance is a gate input)
-- FORK: s 76E(1) | the bar is a SHANT of the company with a BREACH where the purchase is made without advance authority, although the text states no consequence | no breach, the purchase being merely unauthorised
-- src:8890 | 76E.—(1) A company must not make a purchase or acquisition of
-- src:8891 | its own shares on a securities exchange (called in this section a market
-- src:8892 | purchase) unless the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in
-- src:8893 | advance by the company in general meeting.
@ref s 76E(1) no market purchase unless authorised in advance (src:8890-8893)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76E(1) the company must not make a market purchase unless it has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` MEANS
    IF `s 76E(1) the company is barred from making the market purchase` `the purchase or acquisition is made on a securities exchange` `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised in advance by the company in general meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY company
         SHANT `s 76E(1) make a purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares on a securities exchange`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY company BECAUSE "the company made a purchase or acquisition of its own shares on a securities exchange without the advance authority of the company in general meeting that section 76E(1) requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 76F(3): the director who approves a purchase knowing the company is not solvent`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the director or chief executive officer approves or authorises the purchase, acquisition or release; counting=silent (the text puts no time on the offence)
-- FORK: s 76F(3) | the company's insolvency and the person's knowledge of it are gate inputs and the forbidden act is the approval alone | the knowledge inside the act, as "approve ... knowing that the company is not solvent"
-- FORK: s 76F(3) | the existing s 76F(1) gate is called with the payment kind fixed to (1)(a), the payment for acquiring a right with respect to a purchase, although the rule's act also covers a release of obligations; the solvency question of s 76F(4) is the same for each kind | a gate call for each kind of payment
-- FORK: s 76F(3) | the penalty ("a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years", "or" and not "or both") is in the BECAUSE text and not a step | the conviction as a further step
-- src:8978 | (3) Every director or chief executive officer of a company who
-- src:8979 | approves or authorises, the purchase or acquisition of the company’s
-- src:8980 | own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is
-- src:8981 | not solvent shall, without affecting any other liability, be guilty of an
-- src:8982 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:8983 | $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years.
@ref s 76F(3) the offence of approving a purchase knowing the company is not solvent (src:8978-8983)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the company is not solvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76F(3) a director or chief executive officer must not approve or authorise the purchase, acquisition or release knowing that the company is not solvent` MEANS
    IF    (`s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the company is solvent at the date of the payment` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
      AND `the person knows that the company is not solvent`
    THEN PARTY person
         SHANT `s 76F(3) approve or authorise the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY person BECAUSE "the director or chief executive officer approved or authorised the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company was not solvent, and is guilty of an offence, liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 76K(1D): the directors' notice of a cancellation or disposal of treasury shares`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the public company cancels or disposes of the treasury shares; counting="within 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares", the integer line being the count of days with the last day day 30 (sg-periods P1, P2)
-- FORK: s 76K(1D) | the notice is owed by Director "D" for all the directors, and only by a public company: a private company's notice under s 76K(1A) is the means by which it cancels or disposes, with no time and no duty | the private company's lodging as a MUST with no clock
-- src:9197 | (1D) Where a public company cancels or disposes treasury shares
-- src:9198 | in accordance with subsection (1C), the directors of the company
-- src:9199 | must lodge with the Registrar a prescribed notice of the cancellation
-- src:9200 | or disposal of treasury shares together with the prescribed fee within
-- src:9201 | 30 days after the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares.
@ref s 76K(1D) the public company's notice of the cancellation or disposal (src:9197-9201)
GIVEN directors IS A Party
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `share buy-back act`
`s 76K(1D) after the cancellation or disposal the directors of a public company lodge the prescribed notice` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN PARTY directors
         MUST `s 76K(1D) lodge a prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares with the Registrar together with the prescribed fee`
         WITHIN 30
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY directors BECAUSE "the directors of the public company did not lodge the prescribed notice of the cancellation or disposal of treasury shares within 30 days after the cancellation or disposal"
    ELSE FULFILLED

